# Project: conversational search over product manuals and forums

## How to work with me
I'm learning AI/RAG engineering through this project. Before implementing any
retrieval, chunking, embedding, or parsing change, explain the design choice,
the alternatives, and the tradeoffs in 3-5 bullets.
- Do not add LangChain, LlamaIndex, or other frameworks without asking.
- Keep every pipeline choice configurable via YAML in configs/.
- Every new retrieval strategy must be runnable through eval_retrieval.py.
- Prefer small, single-purpose scripts I can read.

## Environment
- Intel Mac (x86_64), macOS 26. Python 3.12 in .venv, managed with uv
  (use `uv pip install`, not pip).
- No Homebrew. Prefer packages with prebuilt Intel-Mac wheels; avoid PyTorch.
- OCR: ocrmac (Apple's built-in text recognition). Vision: Claude API.
- API key lives in .env (loaded with python-dotenv). Never print or hardcode it.

## Project layout
- data/       source PDFs, rendered pages, parsed text
- eval/       questions.jsonl test set
- ingest/     parsing and chunking scripts
- configs/    experiment configs
- results/    experiment results
